{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "03PV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f: X\\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F} $", "MATH_0003": "$X_\\etale$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "MATH_0006": "$$\nf_*\\mathcal{F} : Y_\\etale^{opp} \\longrightarrow \\textit{Sets}, \\quad\n(V/Y) \\longmapsto \\mathcal{F}(X \\times_Y V/X)\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$f_* = f_{small, *}$", "MATH_0008": "$f_{big, *}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{remark-direct-image-sheaf}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-direct-image-sheaf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b72ba3a852348adec100606d18ec181002335ba2e6f34c75ce8937f7f25d5ef3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:278f117b7588f40340bd4a17aaf1de2ac701f9a64216655cad44230b57eded31", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nLet <MATH_0002> a sheaf of sets on <MATH_0003>.\nThe <TEXTITOPEN_0001>direct image<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>, or <TEXTITOPEN_0002>pushforward<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> of <MATH_0004>\n(under <MATH_0005>) is\n<MATH_0006>\nwhich is a sheaf by\nRemark <REF_0001>.\nWe sometimes write <MATH_0007> to distinguish from other\ndirect image functors (such as usual Zariski pushforward or <MATH_0008>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ce5c16f09f9c95e3d5bacabb67ec882bca9fdbd978e46d03fefd9ca7ffdbcab4", "unit_id": "tag:03PY:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03PV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\nf_* = f_{small, *} :\n\\Sh(X_\\etale)\n\\longrightarrow\n\\Sh(Y_\\etale)\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$$\nf_* = f_{small, *} :\n\\textit{Ab}(X_\\etale)\n\\longrightarrow\n\\textit{Ab}(Y_\\etale)\n$$", "MATH_0003": "$f_*$", "MATH_0004": "$0 \\to \\mathcal{F}_1 \\to \\mathcal{F}_2 \\to \\mathcal{F}_3$", "MATH_0005": "$X_\\etale$", "MATH_0006": "$U/X \\in \\Ob(X_\\etale)$", "MATH_0007": "$0 \\to \\mathcal{F}_1(U) \\to \\mathcal{F}_2(U) \\to \\mathcal{F}_3(U)$", "MATH_0008": "$V/Y \\in \\Ob(Y_\\etale)$", "MATH_0009": "$0 \\to f_*\\mathcal{F}_1(V) \\to f_*\\mathcal{F}_2(V) \\to f_*\\mathcal{F}_3(V)$", "MATH_0010": "$U = X \\times_Y V$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{homology-section-functors}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:99c11809a668bd411905afe6d96c30bd0dc1188bc7060073882f36856d668112", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8f37839c6d8bd86266d447d3827e5c9a24ce4c108d947c00ffbabac0860a6aba", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe exact same discussion as above applies and we obtain functors\n<MATH_0001>\nand\n<MATH_0002>\ncalled <TEXTITOPEN_0001>direct image<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> again.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nThe functor <MATH_0003> on abelian sheaves is left exact. (See\nHomology, Section <REF_0001>\nfor what it means for a functor between abelian categories to be left exact.)\nNamely, if\n<MATH_0004>\nis exact on <MATH_0005>, then for every\n<MATH_0006>\nthe sequence of abelian groups\n<MATH_0007>\nis exact. Hence for every <MATH_0008>\nthe sequence of abelian groups\n<MATH_0009>\nis exact, because this is the previous sequence with <MATH_0010>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b8d35d46f94b3eb1f58623a0ab143a4c82448fb85ad09be6d19b2441bc1b0117", "unit_id": "tag:03PV:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "03PV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f: X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{R^pf_*\\}_{p \\geq 1}$", "MATH_0003": "$f_* : \\textit{Ab}(X_\\etale) \\to \\textit{Ab}(Y_\\etale)$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-higher-direct-images}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:044b5db7daa9f18108c30a2f8d99fd069f6209c008fa6c124ea510ea616aac6b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:893e9eb5379b4ebc8b27757262f259d6180068429ed285024e79c6f95bff8c4d", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nThe right derived functors <MATH_0002> of\n<MATH_0003>\nare called <TEXTITOPEN_0001>higher direct images<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:12e616ded6572cd0f1965046e1d38850376c955b4cc8a7b189615bbc0a6698b5", "unit_id": "tag:04I2:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03PV", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e810950cea6e1bdef6960fab4d3899639598231cbb318032343fdc246c37287c", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe higher direct images and their derived category variants are\ndiscussed in more detail in (insert future reference here).\n\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:567c12cb868d60eebf1b13d12f49ede03ea8308f2d00350fd737459f080a4291", "unit_id": "tag:03PV:prose-0004"}
